## Runtime Shell Rules

- Core code uses `RuntimeContext` capabilities and must not depend on concrete infrastructure adapters.
- Controllers live in the server module only.
- Web UI data access goes through repositories backed by `HttpCapability`; no raw `fetch` usage is generated.
- UI components are obtained from the injected UI capability via `useUI()`.
- Tenant IDs are required runtime data and are not defaulted in SQL migrations.

